{"name":"Talismanic Teal","hex":"#159f9b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"talismanic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or similar to, a talisman.","Possessing or believed to possess protective magical power."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/talismanic"},{"term":"teal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small freshwater ducks of the genus Anas that are brightly coloured and have short necks.","A dark, somewhat bluish-green colour; a dark cyan."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Talisman","blocks":[{"text":"A talisman is any object ascribed with religious or magical powers intended to protect, heal, or harm individuals for whom they are made. Talismans are often portable objects carried on someone in a variety of ways, but can also be installed permanently in architecture. Talismans are closely linked with amulets, fulfilling many of the same roles, but a key difference is in their functions. An amulet protects a person or possession against evil forces while a talisman provides good fortune."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Talisman_de_Charlemagne_Tau.jpg/330px-Talisman_de_Charlemagne_Tau.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talisman"},{"title":"Teal","blocks":[{"text":"Teal is a dark cyan color. Its name comes from that of a bird, the Eurasian teal which has a similarly colored stripe on its head. The word is often used colloquially to refer to shades of cyan in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg/330px-Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Roman_golden_ring_with_an_evil_eye_protective_talisman%2C_Vinkovci_Municipal_Museum_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Roman_golden_ring_with_an_evil_eye_protective_talisman%2C_Vinkovci_Municipal_Museum_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Roman_golden_ring_with_an_evil_eye_protective_talisman%2C_Vinkovci_Municipal_Museum_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Roman_golden_ring_with_an_evil_eye_protective_talisman%2C_Vinkovci_Municipal_Museum_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Colonia Aurelia Cibalae 3rd century ring with an evil eye talisman. City Museum of Vinkovci, Croatia[1]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoman_golden_ring_with_an_evil_eye_protective_talisman%2C_Vinkovci_Municipal_Museum_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/OHM_-_Breverl.jpg/500px-OHM_-_Breverl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/OHM_-_Breverl.jpg/1280px-OHM_-_Breverl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/OHM_-_Breverl.jpg/500px-OHM_-_Breverl.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Christian talisman (Breverl), 18th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOHM_-_Breverl.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Khalili_Collection_Islamic_Art_tls_0053.jpg/500px-Khalili_Collection_Islamic_Art_tls_0053.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org